# Exact downstream request bytes, in order (step dividers)

### step 1: PUT http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/logging-to-file (enable file logging)
PUT /v0/management/logging-to-file HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 14


{"value":true}

### step 2: GET http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/logging-to-file (toggle read back)
GET /v0/management/logging-to-file HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1




### step 3: GET http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/logs?limit=3 (log lines shape)
GET /v0/management/logs?limit=3 HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1




### step 4: DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/logs (clear logs)
DELETE /v0/management/logs HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1




### step 5: PUT http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/logging-to-file (disable file logging)
PUT /v0/management/logging-to-file HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 15


{"value":false}

### step 6: GET http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/logs (disabled again)
GET /v0/management/logs HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1



